WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:07.588
In the Encyclopedia of Triangle Centers, Circle Inversion is the conformal radial reflection across a circle of radius R.

2
00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:18.370
A point P at distance d from the center O maps to a point P prime along the same ray O P at distance R squared over d, so that the product of their radial distances equals R squared.

3
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:33.960
In Collection One, inversion in the Circumcircle centered at X three maps the First Isodynamic Point X fifteen inside the triangle directly onto the Second Isodynamic Point X sixteen outside the triangle along the Brocard axis.

4
00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:44.460
Because the three Apollonian circles pass through both X fifteen and X sixteen, each Apollonian circle is orthogonal to the circumcircle and invariant under circumcircle inversion.
